# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metalpicture.willow), on the willow.
#
# rc.jobs.metalpicture at the willow's panel: 64 of Apple's clearFragment shaders in an 8x8 mosaic and
# Apple's textured blit in two bands, every pixel computed by this port's Metal driver on the Adreno 610
# and copied to the panel by the kernel (kRedwoodShow). metal_drv_test takes the panel's size from
# device=willow: 1080x2340, tiles of 135x130 (1040 rows), the two bands 648 each as on redwood, the
# last four rows black. See rc.jobs.metalpicture for what each line of the log means.
#
# Build with JOBS="" WIFID=0 GL=1: no daemon of Apple's, so the home screen does not draw over the
# picture, and GL=1 for /redwood/lib/libredwoodair.dylib. The waits are cpu_test's, not rwtouch's:
# on the willow rwtouch does not come back from opening /dev/redwood-touch.
#
# 1. The canary: clearFragment20 into a 4x4 attachment, whose pixels have softpipe's reference.
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --draw /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
#
# 2. The picture, repainted for 90 seconds: the mosaic first, then the ladder, then the two bands.
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --picture 90 /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
